{% doc %}
  Wheel search for WHEEL collections — the counterpart to
  pt-collection-research-strip, which searches TIRES.

  Why this exists: the tire strip was rendering on wheel collections, where it
  can only ever return nothing. Wheels carry custom.bolt_pattern / rim_diameter
  / rim_width / rim_offset / center_bore and NOT custom.tire_width or
  tire_profile (measured 2026-09-27: 0 of 2,061 wheel products have a tire
  metafield), so a tire-size search there is zero results by construction.

  Two tabs:
    - By vehicle: year / make / model off the same pt-vehicle-{year}.json assets
      every other vehicle surface uses, then /api/wheel-fitment for the car's
      bolt pattern and OE rim diameters, then a facet URL.
    - By wheel specs: diameter / bolt pattern / width / offset, with every
      option and count taken from `collection.filters` so an option can never
      show zero results and the strings always match what Shopify indexed.

  BOLT PATTERNS ARE MULTI-VALUE. A wheel drilled for two patterns is stored as
  one string, "6x135/6x139.7". Shopify facets match the WHOLE string, so asking
  for "6x139.7" finds 20 wheels when 219 actually fit. Every canonical PCD is
  therefore expanded to every catalogue string containing it, and the list of
  catalogue strings comes from the live facet rather than a hardcoded array —
  the hardcoded-list mistake is what limited the homepage search to a handful
  of results.

  CENTRE BORE IS DELIBERATELY NOT FILTERED. A wheel fits when its bore is >=
  the hub; a centring ring covers the difference. Filtering on it excluded
  valid wheels and was the other half of the homepage under-matching.

  USABLE OFF A COLLECTION PAGE TOO. Only a collection page has
  `collection.filters`, so when none is passed (the homepage hero) the spec
  options are fetched once, lazily, from /collections/wheels?view=facets — the
  JSON view of Shopify's own facet index. Same data, one source; copying the
  catalogue's values into a second surface is how the old hardcoded bore list
  rotted until it hid ~1,100 of ~1,400 wheels.

  @param {collection} [collection] - The current collection, when on one.
  @param {string} [target] - Collection path to search. Defaults to /collections/wheels
                             so a brand collection still searches the whole catalogue.
  @param {string} [facets_url] - Where to fetch facets when there is no collection.
  @param {boolean} [compact] - Tighter styling for the hero.
  @param {boolean} [show_counts] - false: spec options print no product counts and
                                   options with 0 products are left out (the results
                                   header, owner decision 5). Default true.
  @param {string} [msg_target] - CSS selector of an element OUTSIDE any collapsible
                                 panel; the "Need tires too?" box and the "we don't
                                 stock that bolt pattern" message go there instead of
                                 next to the widget, so a closed panel can't hide them.
  @param {string} [package_url] - Package mode (the hero's Packages tab): vehicle only,
                                  no spec tab or collapse toggle, an extra Trim select,
                                  and the button goes to this URL with ?y=&mk=&md=&tr=
                                  instead of searching wheels.

  @example
  {% render 'pt-wheel-search', collection: collection %}
  {% render 'pt-wheel-search', compact: true %}
  {% render 'pt-wheel-search', compact: true, package_url: '/pages/wheel-package' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign target_path = target | default: '/collections/wheels'
  assign ws_counts = true
  if show_counts == false
    assign ws_counts = false
  endif
  assign f_bolt = ''
  assign f_dia = ''
  assign f_width = ''
  assign f_offset = ''
  for f in collection.filters
    if f.param_name == 'filter.p.m.custom.bolt_pattern'
      assign f_bolt = f
    elsif f.param_name == 'filter.p.m.custom.rim_diameter'
      assign f_dia = f
    elsif f.param_name == 'filter.p.m.custom.rim_width'
      assign f_width = f
    elsif f.param_name == 'filter.p.m.custom.rim_offset'
      assign f_offset = f
    endif
  endfor
  assign has_specs = false
  if f_bolt != '' and f_dia != ''
    assign has_specs = true
  endif
  comment
    No collection to read filters from (the hero): render the spec tab anyway
    and let the script fill its dropdowns from ?view=facets on first click.
  endcomment
  assign facets_src = facets_url | default: '/collections/wheels?view=facets'
  assign lazy_specs = false
  if has_specs == false
    assign lazy_specs = true
    assign has_specs = true
  endif
  comment
    Package mode needs only the car: the builder works out wheels and tires
    itself, so no spec tab and no facet fetch.
  endcomment
  assign pkg_mode = false
  if package_url != blank
    assign pkg_mode = true
    assign has_specs = false
    assign lazy_specs = false
  endif
-%}

{% render 'pt-vehicle-manifest-loader' %}

<div
  class="pt-ws{% if compact %} pt-ws--compact{% endif %}{% if pkg_mode %} pt-ws--package{% endif %}"
  data-pt-ws
  data-target="{{ target_path }}"
  data-facets-url="{{ facets_src }}"
  {% if lazy_specs %}data-lazy-specs="1"{% endif %}{% unless ws_counts %} data-no-counts="1"{% endunless %}{% if msg_target != blank %} data-msg-target="{{ msg_target | escape }}"{% endif %}{% if pkg_mode %} data-package-url="{{ package_url | escape }}"{% endif %}
  data-api-base="{{ settings.chat_api_base | default: 'https://app.princetires.ca' }}"
  data-asset-base="{{ 'pt-vehicle-2025.json' | asset_url | split: 'pt-vehicle-2025.json' | first }}"
  data-asset-version="{%- assign _au = 'pt-vehicle-2025.json' | asset_url -%}{%- if _au contains '?' -%}{{ _au | split: '?' | last }}{%- endif -%}"
  data-manifest-url="{{ 'pt-vehicle-manifest.json' | asset_url }}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    Every bolt_pattern string Shopify has indexed for this collection, so the
    expansion below is always in step with the catalogue.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="application/json" data-pt-ws-bolts>
    [
      {%- if f_bolt != '' -%}
        {%- for v in f_bolt.values -%}
          {"v": {{ v.label | json }}, "n": {{ v.count }}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    ]
  </script>

  {% unless pkg_mode or compact %}<button type="button" class="pt-ws__toggle" data-pt-ws-toggle aria-expanded="false">Find wheels ▾</button>{% endunless %}

  <div class="pt-ws__body" data-pt-ws-body>
    {% unless pkg_mode %}<div class="pt-ws__tabs" role="tablist">
      <button type="button" class="pt-ws__tab is-active" data-pt-ws-tab="vehicle" role="tab" aria-selected="true">By vehicle</button>
      {%- if has_specs -%}
        <button type="button" class="pt-ws__tab" data-pt-ws-tab="specs" role="tab" aria-selected="false">By wheel specs</button>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>{% endunless %}

    <div class="pt-ws__panel is-active" data-pt-ws-panel="vehicle">
      <div class="pt-ws__row">
        <label class="pt-ws__field">
          <span class="pt-ws__label">Year</span>
          <select class="pt-ws__select" data-pt-ws-year>
            <option value="">{% if pkg_mode %}Year{% else %}—{% endif %}</option>
            {%- assign ws_max = settings.smart_search_max_year | default: 2027 | times: 1 -%}
            {%- assign ws_min = settings.smart_search_min_year | default: 1990 | times: 1 -%}
            {%- for i in (ws_min..ws_max) reversed -%}
              <option value="{{ i }}">{{ i }}</option>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </select>
        </label>
        <label class="pt-ws__field">
          <span class="pt-ws__label">Make</span>
          <select class="pt-ws__select" data-pt-ws-make disabled{% if pkg_mode %} data-pt-ws-ph="Make"{% endif %}><option value="">{% if pkg_mode %}Make{% else %}—{% endif %}</option></select>
        </label>
        <label class="pt-ws__field">
          <span class="pt-ws__label">Model</span>
          <select class="pt-ws__select" data-pt-ws-model disabled{% if pkg_mode %} data-pt-ws-ph="Model"{% endif %}><option value="">{% if pkg_mode %}Model{% else %}—{% endif %}</option></select>
        </label>{% if pkg_mode %}
        {%- comment -%}
          The builder only shows packages once it has a trim (it asks for one
          otherwise), so package mode collects it here: same year file, same
          trim names the builder matches against.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <label class="pt-ws__field">
          <span class="pt-ws__label">Trim</span>
          <select class="pt-ws__select" data-pt-ws-trim disabled data-pt-ws-ph="Trim"><option value="">Trim</option></select>
        </label>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="pt-ws__actions">
        <button type="button" class="pt-ws__submit" data-pt-ws-submit-vehicle disabled>{% if pkg_mode %}See my packages{% else %}Find wheels{% endif %}</button>
        <span class="pt-ws__status" data-pt-ws-status></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if has_specs -%}
      <div class="pt-ws__panel" data-pt-ws-panel="specs">
        <p class="pt-ws__hint" data-pt-ws-specs-hint{% unless lazy_specs %} hidden{% endunless %}>Pick any of these — leave the rest on Any.</p>
        <div class="pt-ws__row">
          <label class="pt-ws__field">
            <span class="pt-ws__label">Diameter</span>
            <select class="pt-ws__select" data-pt-ws-spec="rim_diameter" data-unit="&quot;">
              <option value="">Any</option>
              {%- unless lazy_specs -%}{%- for v in f_dia.values -%}{%- if ws_counts -%}<option value="{{ v.label | escape }}">{{ v.label }}" ({{ v.count }})</option>{%- elsif v.count > 0 or v.active -%}<option value="{{ v.label | escape }}">{{ v.label }}"</option>{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endunless -%}
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="pt-ws__field">
            <span class="pt-ws__label">Bolt pattern</span>
            <select class="pt-ws__select" data-pt-ws-spec="bolt_pattern">
              <option value="">Any</option>
              {%- unless lazy_specs -%}{%- for v in f_bolt.values -%}{%- if ws_counts -%}<option value="{{ v.label | escape }}">{{ v.label }} ({{ v.count }})</option>{%- elsif v.count > 0 or v.active -%}<option value="{{ v.label | escape }}">{{ v.label }}</option>{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endunless -%}
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="pt-ws__field">
            <span class="pt-ws__label">Width</span>
            <select class="pt-ws__select" data-pt-ws-spec="rim_width" data-unit="&quot;">
              <option value="">Any</option>
              {%- unless lazy_specs -%}{%- for v in f_width.values -%}{%- if ws_counts -%}<option value="{{ v.label | escape }}">{{ v.label }}" ({{ v.count }})</option>{%- elsif v.count > 0 or v.active -%}<option value="{{ v.label | escape }}">{{ v.label }}"</option>{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endunless -%}
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="pt-ws__field">
            <span class="pt-ws__label">Offset</span>
            <select class="pt-ws__select" data-pt-ws-spec="rim_offset" data-prefix="ET ">
              <option value="">Any</option>
              {%- unless lazy_specs -%}{%- for v in f_offset.values -%}{%- if ws_counts -%}<option value="{{ v.label | escape }}">ET {{ v.label }} ({{ v.count }})</option>{%- elsif v.count > 0 or v.active -%}<option value="{{ v.label | escape }}">ET {{ v.label }}</option>{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endunless -%}
            </select>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="pt-ws__actions">
          <button type="button" class="pt-ws__submit" data-pt-ws-submit-specs>Search</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% javascript %}
  (function () {
    // One closure per instance: the homepage hero renders this snippet twice
    // (Wheels tab + Packages tab), and a page-wide querySelector would leave
    // the second one dead. Everything below is scoped to its own root.
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-pt-ws]').forEach(init);

    function init(root) {
      var target = root.dataset.target || '/collections/wheels';
      var apiBase = root.dataset.apiBase || '';
      var assetBase = root.dataset.assetBase || '';
      var assetVersion = root.dataset.assetVersion || '';
      var manifestUrl = root.dataset.manifestUrl || '';
      var facetsUrl = root.dataset.facetsUrl || '/collections/wheels?view=facets';
      var lazySpecs = root.dataset.lazySpecs === '1';
      var pkgUrl = root.dataset.packageUrl || '';
      var noCounts = root.dataset.noCounts === '1';
      // Where the cross-sell / bolt-hint message goes (outside a collapsible panel).
      function msgSlot() {
        var sel = root.dataset.msgTarget;
        if (!sel) return null;
        try { return document.querySelector(sel); } catch (e) { return null; }
      }
      var F = 'filter.p.m.custom.';

      var catalogBolts = [];
      try {
        var node = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-bolts]');
        catalogBolts = node ? JSON.parse(node.textContent) : [];
      } catch (e) { catalogBolts = []; }

      var elYear = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-year]');
      var elMake = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-make]');
      var elModel = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-model]');
      var elTrim = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-trim]'); // package mode only
      var elGo = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-submit-vehicle]');
      var elStatus = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-status]');
      var elToggle = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-toggle]');
      var elBody = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-body]');

      var yearData = null, manifest = null, loadingYear = null;

      function status(m) { if (elStatus) elStatus.textContent = m || ''; }

      function fill(sel, placeholder, values) {
        sel.innerHTML = '';
        var o = document.createElement('option');
        o.value = ''; o.textContent = placeholder;
        sel.appendChild(o);
        values.forEach(function (v) {
          var opt = document.createElement('option');
          opt.value = v; opt.textContent = v;
          sel.appendChild(opt);
        });
        sel.disabled = values.length === 0;
      }
      // Package mode names its empty selects (its labels are hidden on phones).
      function reset(sel) { sel.innerHTML = '<option value="">' + (sel.getAttribute('data-pt-ws-ph') || '—') + '</option>'; sel.disabled = true; }
      // A trim is required only when the year file lists some (package mode).
      function sync() { elGo.disabled = !(elYear.value && elMake.value && elModel.value && (!elTrim || elTrim.disabled || elTrim.value)); }

      // Off a collection page there is no collection.filters, so pull the same
      // data from Shopify's facet index as JSON. Once per page, cached for the
      // session; a failure leaves the tab usable with "Any" everywhere.
      var facetsPromise = null;
      function loadFacets() {
        if (facetsPromise) return facetsPromise;
        var cached = null;
        try { cached = JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem('pt-ws-facets') || 'null'); } catch (e) {}
        facetsPromise = cached
          ? Promise.resolve(cached)
          // NO Accept: application/json here — that header makes Shopify return its
          // own built-in collection JSON instead of rendering the ?view= template.
          : fetch(facetsUrl)
              .then(function (r) { if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status); return r.json(); })
              .then(function (j) { try { sessionStorage.setItem('pt-ws-facets', JSON.stringify(j)); } catch (e) {} return j; })
              .catch(function () { return null; });
        return facetsPromise;
      }

      function applyFacets(j) {
        if (!j || !Array.isArray(j.filters)) return;
        var by = {};
        j.filters.forEach(function (f) { by[f.param] = f.values || []; });
        root.querySelectorAll('[data-pt-ws-spec]').forEach(function (sel) {
          if (sel.options.length > 1) return; // already filled
          var vals = by[F + sel.dataset.ptWsSpec] || [];
          var prefix = sel.dataset.prefix || '';
          var unit = sel.dataset.unit || '';
          vals.forEach(function (v) {
            if (noCounts && !(Number(v.n) > 0)) return;
            var o = document.createElement('option');
            o.value = v.v;
            o.textContent = prefix + v.v + unit + (noCounts ? '' : ' (' + v.n + ')');
            sel.appendChild(o);
          });
          sel.disabled = vals.length === 0;
        });
        // the bolt list the vehicle search expands against
        if (!catalogBolts.length) catalogBolts = (by[F + 'bolt_pattern'] || []).slice();
        var hint = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-specs-hint]');
        if (hint) hint.hidden = false;
      }

      if (lazySpecs) loadFacets().then(applyFacets);

      if (elToggle) elToggle.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var open = root.classList.toggle('is-open');
        elToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'true' : 'false');
      });

      root.querySelectorAll('[data-pt-ws-tab]').forEach(function (tab) {
        tab.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var name = tab.dataset.ptWsTab;
          root.querySelectorAll('[data-pt-ws-tab]').forEach(function (t) {
            var on = t === tab;
            t.classList.toggle('is-active', on);
            t.setAttribute('aria-selected', on ? 'true' : 'false');
          });
          root.querySelectorAll('[data-pt-ws-panel]').forEach(function (p) {
            p.classList.toggle('is-active', p.dataset.ptWsPanel === name);
          });
        });
      });

      function loadYear(year, wantMake, wantModel, wantTrim) {
        yearData = null; reset(elMake); reset(elModel); if (elTrim) reset(elTrim); sync();
        if (!year) return Promise.resolve();
        loadingYear = year;
        var url = window.PTVehicleManifest
          ? window.PTVehicleManifest.yearUrl(assetBase, year, manifest, assetVersion)
          : assetBase + 'pt-vehicle-' + year + '.json' + (assetVersion ? '?' + assetVersion : '');
        return fetch(url, { cache: 'force-cache' })
          .then(function (r) { if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status); return r.json(); })
          .then(function (data) {
            if (loadingYear !== year) return;
            yearData = data;
            fill(elMake, 'Make', (data.makes || Object.keys(data.models || {})).slice().sort());
            if (wantMake) { elMake.value = wantMake; if (elMake.value) fillModels(wantMake, wantModel, wantTrim); }
            sync();
          })
          .catch(function () { if (loadingYear === year) status("Couldn't load vehicles for " + year + '.'); });
      }

      function fillModels(make, wantModel, wantTrim) {
        reset(elModel);
        if (elTrim) reset(elTrim);
        if (!make || !yearData) { sync(); return; }
        fill(elModel, 'Model', Object.keys((yearData.models || {})[make] || {}).sort());
        if (wantModel) { elModel.value = wantModel; if (elTrim && elModel.value) fillTrims(make, wantModel, wantTrim); }
        sync();
      }

      // Package mode: trims in the year file's own order (the builder's
      // order); a single trim is picked for the shopper.
      function fillTrims(make, model, wantTrim) {
        reset(elTrim);
        if (make && model && yearData) {
          var trims = Object.keys(((yearData.models || {})[make] || {})[model] || {});
          fill(elTrim, 'Trim', trims);
          if (trims.length === 1) elTrim.value = trims[0];
          else if (wantTrim) elTrim.value = wantTrim;
        }
        sync();
      }

      elYear.addEventListener('change', function () { status(''); loadYear(elYear.value); });
      elMake.addEventListener('change', function () { status(''); fillModels(elMake.value); });
      elModel.addEventListener('change', function () { status(''); if (elTrim) fillTrims(elMake.value, elModel.value); else sync(); });
      if (elTrim) elTrim.addEventListener('change', sync);

      // "6x139.7" -> every catalogue string drilled for it, e.g.
      // ["6x139.7", "6x135/6x139.7", "6x120/6x139.7"].
      function expandBolt(pcd) {
        if (!pcd) return [];
        var want = String(pcd).trim().toLowerCase();
        return catalogBolts
          .filter(function (b) {
            return String(b.v).toLowerCase().split('/').some(function (part) { return part.trim() === want; });
          })
          .map(function (b) { return b.v; });
      }

      function goVehicle() {
        var year = elYear.value, make = elMake.value, model = elModel.value;
        if (!year || !make || !model) return;
        if (pkgUrl) {
          // Package mode: the builder looks the car up itself. Hand over the
          // names exactly as pt-vehicle-{year}.json spells them — the builder
          // reads the same files and matches y / mk / md / tr case-insensitively.
          var trim = elTrim ? elTrim.value : '';
          window.location.href = pkgUrl + (pkgUrl.indexOf('?') === -1 ? '?' : '&') +
            'y=' + encodeURIComponent(year) + '&mk=' + encodeURIComponent(make) + '&md=' + encodeURIComponent(model) +
            (trim ? '&tr=' + encodeURIComponent(trim) : '');
          return;
        }
        elGo.disabled = true;
        status('Finding wheels for your ' + year + ' ' + make + ' ' + model + '…');
        // Off a collection page the catalogue's bolt strings arrive with the
        // facets, so make sure they are here before expanding the car's PCD —
        // otherwise every car looks like one we stock nothing for.
        var ready = catalogBolts.length ? Promise.resolve() : loadFacets().then(applyFacets);
        ready
          .then(function () { return fetch(apiBase + '/api/wheel-fitment?year=' + encodeURIComponent(year) + '&make=' + encodeURIComponent(make) + '&model=' + encodeURIComponent(model)); })
          .then(function (r) { return r.json(); })
          .then(function (d) {
            var bolts = expandBolt(d && d.bolt_pattern);
            if (!bolts.length) {
              // Either we have no spec for the car, or we stock nothing in its
              // pattern. Say which — never send the shopper to an empty grid.
              status(d && d.bolt_pattern
                ? "We don't stock wheels in your " + d.bolt_pattern + " bolt pattern — ask us and we can order them."
                : "We don't have wheel specs for that vehicle yet — ask us in chat.");
              elGo.disabled = false;
              return;
            }
            var qs = [];
            bolts.forEach(function (b) { qs.push(F + 'bolt_pattern=' + encodeURIComponent(b)); });
            var dias = [];
            (d.wheel_sizes || []).forEach(function (w) {
              if (w && w.diameter && dias.indexOf(String(w.diameter)) === -1) dias.push(String(w.diameter));
            });
            dias.forEach(function (x) { qs.push(F + 'rim_diameter=' + encodeURIComponent(x)); });
            var oeTire = (d.tire_sizes || [])[0] || '';
            try {
              localStorage.setItem('pt-tire-search-vehicle', JSON.stringify({
                year: year, make: make, model: model, trim: '',
                tireSize: oeTire, savedAt: new Date().toISOString()
              }));
              // Tells the results page to offer tires for the car just searched.
              sessionStorage.setItem('pt-ws-crosssell', JSON.stringify({
                year: year, make: make, model: model, tireSize: oeTire
              }));
              // Lets the results page confirm the fit ("Showing wheels with the
              // 5x114.3 bolt pattern your 2021 Honda CR-V uses") while these
              // exact bolt filters stay applied (assets/pt-rd-results.js).
              sessionStorage.setItem('pt-ws-fit', JSON.stringify({
                label: year + ' ' + make + ' ' + model, bolt: d.bolt_pattern, bolts: bolts
              }));
            } catch (e) {}
            window.location.href = target + '?' + qs.join('&');
          })
          .catch(function () { status("Couldn't look that up just now — please try again."); elGo.disabled = false; });
      }
      elGo.addEventListener('click', goVehicle);

      var elSpecGo = root.querySelector('[data-pt-ws-submit-specs]');
      if (elSpecGo) {
        elSpecGo.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var qs = [];
          root.querySelectorAll('[data-pt-ws-spec]').forEach(function (sel) {
            if (sel.value) qs.push(F + sel.dataset.ptWsSpec + '=' + encodeURIComponent(sel.value));
          });
          window.location.href = qs.length ? target + '?' + qs.join('&') : target;
        });
      }

      // ?pt_bolt=6x139.7 — a raw vehicle bolt pattern handed over by another
      // surface (the homepage "wheels that fit" CTA). Expand it against the live
      // facet here, where the catalogue list lives, and rewrite the URL to real
      // filters. Keeps ONE expansion implementation; a copy elsewhere would go
      // stale, which is exactly how the old hardcoded bore list broke.
      function applyBoltHint() {
        var p = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
        var hint = p.get('pt_bolt');
        if (!hint) return false;
        var bolts = expandBolt(hint);
        p.delete('pt_bolt');
        if (!bolts.length) {
          // Nothing in stock drilled that way — say so rather than showing an
          // unfiltered grid that looks like it answered the question.
          root.classList.add('is-open');
          var noBolt = "We don't stock wheels in your " + hint + ' bolt pattern — ask us and we can order them.';
          status(noBolt);
          var slot = msgSlot();
          if (slot) {
            var m = document.createElement('div');
            m.className = 'pt-ws__crosssell pt-ws__nobolt';
            m.setAttribute('role', 'status');
            m.textContent = noBolt;
            slot.appendChild(m);
          }
          if (window.history && window.history.replaceState) {
            window.history.replaceState({}, '', window.location.pathname + (p.toString() ? '?' + p : ''));
          }
          return false;
        }
        bolts.forEach(function (b) { p.append(F + 'bolt_pattern', b); });
        window.location.replace(window.location.pathname + '?' + p.toString());
        return true;
      }

      // Prefill from the car the shopper already gave us on another surface.
      function start() {
        var saved = null;
        try {
          var raw = localStorage.getItem('pt-tire-search-vehicle');
          saved = raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : null;
        } catch (e) { saved = null; }
        if (!saved || !saved.year || !saved.make || !saved.model) return;
        var y = String(saved.year);
        if (!Array.prototype.some.call(elYear.options, function (o) { return o.value === y; })) return;
        elYear.value = y;
        loadYear(y, String(saved.make), String(saved.model), saved.trim ? String(saved.trim) : '').then(function () {
          // Package mode skips this line: the filled selects already show the
          // car, and the extra line made the always-open panel taller.
          if (pkgUrl) return;
          if (elYear.value && elMake.value && elModel.value) status('Your ' + y + ' ' + saved.make + ' ' + saved.model + ' — hit Find wheels.');
        });
      }

      // "Want tires too?" — shown on the RESULTS page, after a by-vehicle wheel
      // search, because that is the moment the shopper has the car in mind and
      // has seen the wheels. One-click, using the OE size we already looked up.
      function offerTires() {
        var raw = null;
        try { raw = sessionStorage.getItem('pt-ws-crosssell'); } catch (e) { return; }
        if (!raw) return;
        try { sessionStorage.removeItem('pt-ws-crosssell'); } catch (e) {}
        var v;
        try { v = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { return; }
        if (!v || !v.year || !v.make || !v.model) return;
        var label = v.year + ' ' + v.make + ' ' + v.model;
        var href = v.tireSize
          ? '/collections/tires?' + F + 'tire_size=' + encodeURIComponent(v.tireSize)
          : '/collections/tires';
        var box = document.createElement('div');
        box.className = 'pt-ws__crosssell';
        box.innerHTML =
          '<span>Need tires for your <strong></strong> too?' +
          (v.tireSize ? ' Factory size <strong class="pt-ws__xs-size"></strong>.' : '') +
          '</span><a class="pt-ws__xs-cta" href="' + href + '">Find tires →</a>' +
          '<button type="button" class="pt-ws__xs-no" aria-label="Dismiss">No thanks</button>';
        box.querySelector('strong').textContent = label;
        var sz = box.querySelector('.pt-ws__xs-size');
        if (sz) sz.textContent = v.tireSize;
        box.querySelector('.pt-ws__xs-no').addEventListener('click', function () { box.remove(); });
        var slot = msgSlot();
        if (slot) slot.appendChild(box);
        else root.parentNode.insertBefore(box, root.nextSibling);
      }

      // The bolt hint is a redirect, so resolve it before anything else loads.
      // Neither applies to package mode (no wheel results page behind it).
      if (!pkgUrl) {
        if (applyBoltHint()) return;
        offerTires();
      }

      if (window.PTVehicleManifest) {
        window.PTVehicleManifest.ready(manifestUrl, 1500).then(function (m) {
          manifest = m;
          if (m) window.PTVehicleManifest.fillYearSelect(elYear, window.PTVehicleManifest.yearsDesc(m));
          start();
        });
      } else { start(); }
    }
  })();
{% endjavascript %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .pt-ws { margin: 0 0 1.6rem; border: 1px solid #e2e8ed; border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; }
  .pt-ws__toggle { display: none; width: 100%; padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem; border: 0; background: none; font: inherit; font-weight: 600; text-align: left; cursor: pointer; color: #1f2a33; }
  .pt-ws__body { padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem 1.2rem; }
  .pt-ws__tabs { display: flex; gap: 1.6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #e8edf1; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
  .pt-ws__tab { border: 0; background: none; padding: 0 0 0.8rem; font: inherit; font-size: 1.4rem; color: #5a6873; cursor: pointer; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; margin-bottom: -1px; }
  .pt-ws__tab.is-active { color: #b9221a; font-weight: 700; border-bottom-color: #b9221a; }
  .pt-ws__panel { display: none; }
  .pt-ws__panel.is-active { display: block; }
  .pt-ws__row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 0.8rem; }
  .pt-ws__field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; min-width: 0; }
  .pt-ws__label { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #5a6873; }
  .pt-ws__select { height: 44px; padding: 0 0.7rem; border: 1px solid #cdd6dd; border-radius: 8px; font-family: inherit; font-size: 1.4rem; background: #fff; color: #1f2a33; }
  .pt-ws__select:disabled { background: #f1f4f6; color: #8a97a1; }
  .pt-ws__select:focus { outline: none; border-color: #b9221a; }
  /* iOS Safari zooms the page when a control under 16px is tapped. */
  @media (max-width: 749px) { .pt-ws__select { font-size: 16px; } }
  .pt-ws__actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .pt-ws__submit { height: 44px; padding: 0 2rem; border: 0; border-radius: 8px; cursor: pointer; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #DA291C, #b9221a); color: #fff; font-family: inherit; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.4rem; }
  .pt-ws__submit:disabled { opacity: 0.55; cursor: default; }
  .pt-ws__status { font-size: 1.3rem; color: #5a6873; }
  .pt-ws__hint { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; font-size: 1.25rem; color: #5a6873; }
  .pt-ws__crosssell { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 0 0 1.6rem; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; border: 1px solid #f0d8a8; background: #fffaf0; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 1.35rem; color: #5a4a2f; }
  .pt-ws__xs-cta { font-weight: 700; color: #b9221a; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pt-ws__xs-cta:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .pt-ws__xs-no { margin-left: auto; border: 0; background: none; color: #8a97a1; font: inherit; font-size: 1.2rem; cursor: pointer; }
  /* Hero: the panel sits on a dark photo, so invert the chrome. */
  .pt-ws--compact { border: 0; background: transparent; margin: 0; }
  .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__body { padding: 0; }
  .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__tab { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72); }
  .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__tab.is-active { color: #fff; border-bottom-color: #fff; }
  .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__tabs { border-bottom-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.22); justify-content: center; }
  .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__label { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75); }
  .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__hint { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75); text-align: center; }
  .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__status { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); }
  .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__actions { justify-content: center; }
  /* Package mode: always open (no toggle). One grid for the four selects AND
     the button, so the trim costs no extra row: Year / Make / Model, then Trim
     beside "See my packages". Three across keeps names readable. */
  .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__body { display: block; }
  .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__panel.is-active { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.8rem; align-items: end; }
  .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__row { display: contents; }
  .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__field:nth-child(4) { grid-column: span 2; }
  .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__actions { margin-top: 0; }
  .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__submit { width: 100%; padding: 0 1rem; }
  /* Phones: a narrow Year beside a wide Make, then Model and Trim side by side
     (three or four across clips make and model names), then the button. The
     selects name themselves ("Year", "Make"…), so the labels go visually. */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__panel.is-active { grid-template-columns: repeat(10, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__field,
    .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__field:nth-child(4) { grid-column: span 5; }
    .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__field:first-child { grid-column: span 3; }
    .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__field:nth-child(2) { grid-column: span 7; }
    .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__actions { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .pt-ws--package .pt-ws__label { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; margin: -1px; padding: 0; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .pt-ws__toggle { display: block; }
    .pt-ws__body { display: none; }
    .pt-ws.is-open .pt-ws__body { display: block; }
    /* Hero (compact): the WHEELS pill is already the opener, so no second
       dark-on-dark collapse. The /collections/wheels card keeps its toggle. */
    .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__toggle { display: none; }
    .pt-ws--compact .pt-ws__body { display: block; }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
